Hide the SYSVIPC fields added by 001 from bindgen

Patch 001 puts sysvsem/sysvshm into a padding hole of task_struct inside
__kabi_ignored unions, which gendwarfksyms ignores for C. bindgen still
turns them into new members and union types of bindings::task_struct, so
the CRCs of Rust kernel-crate exports that reach task_struct change, and
the extra impls renumber other Rust symbols. __BINDGEN__ is defined only
while bindgen runs, so Rust keeps seeing the stock task_struct layout.
The fields sit in padding, so the layout Rust sees is unchanged.

diff --git a/include/linux/sched.h b/include/linux/sched.h
index af6712f..794b76c 100644
--- a/include/linux/sched.h
+++ b/include/linux/sched.h
@@ -885,7 +885,7 @@ struct task_struct {
 	int				normal_prio;
 	unsigned int			rt_priority;
 
-#ifdef CONFIG_SYSVIPC
+#if defined(CONFIG_SYSVIPC) && !defined(__BINDGEN__)
 	union {
 		char __kabi_ignored_0;
 		struct sysv_sem			sysvsem;
